ed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'm using the latest dev revision and I've noticed some unpleasant memory effect that was not present in r68. It happens when meshes (geometry/texture/material) are added and deleted.\n\nTo reproduce it, you could just use the standard memory example: [webgl_test_memory](http://threejs.org/examples/#webgl_test_memory) with the latest dev revision of threejs.\n\nWhen I try this example in my local environment, I get ~500Mb heap profiles in ~10 seconds after I load the example. The profiler shows something like this:\n\n![profiler pic](http://i57.tinypic.com/2vl65ax.jpg)\n","closed_by":{"login":"goodsign","id":3010927,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMTA5Mjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3010927?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign","html_url":"https://github.com/goodsign","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goodsign/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5269/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}